# Product truth

- Do not infer certs from organic fibre. Organic ≠ GOTS.
- Mill programme ≠ quality claim. Missing evidence stays missing.
- Do not generate article IDs. Empty article is an exception.
- Do not overwrite `sourceValue`. Immutable mill source; normalised values sit alongside.
- Do not mark MOQ / lead / price as current without a mill confirmation timestamp.
- Named grants only. Cookie, approve-all, and confidence cannot create Granted visibility.
- Brand-private preferred / proven / excluded memory never leaks across tenants or to mills.
- Agents operate on bounded source pointers — never the whole corpus in an LLM prompt.
- Destinations are projections; they must not mutate source truth.
